# Declared exemptions for the variant-coverage check
# (every-emitted-variant-has-a-witness).
#
# Format: file | symbol | reason
#   file   — basename of the koru_std source whose emitted-string content
#            first carries the symbol (as the check derives it)
#   symbol — the derived marker, placeholders as {} (e.g. __store_write_{})
#   reason — why NO test on this host can witness the symbol, or why the
#            symbol is not really emitted surface (e.g. a startsWith
#            predicate quoted in a string). Mandatory. An entry matching
#            no uncovered symbol is stale and FAILS the check.
#
# An exemption is a ruling that this symbol's invisibility is understood
# and accepted. Everything not listed here is invisible surface: emitter
# code that ships with zero executions behind it.

# --- Not emitted Zig code: markers the scan cannot see by construction ---
runtime.registry.kz | __KORU_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_HELPERS__ | comment-carried dedup sentinel, emitted as `// marker` text — any artifact hit sits inside a comment the scan strips. Was runtime.kz until the ~part registry split moved the constant; attribution followed the move
runtime.registry.kz | __KORU_SCOPE_DEF__                | scope-def marker emitted as a `// __KORU_SCOPE_DEF__` host_line so later `scope(other)` sites resolve order-free; comment-carried, the scan strips it by construction
fmt.kz              | __KORU_INLINE__                   | label placeholder, substituted with a unique per-site label by src/emitter_helpers.zig:4438 before anything is written; it can never reach an artifact verbatim
kernel.kz           | __koru_self_elem_{}               | substitution sentinel, never emitted even on a successful run: kernel.kz:1944-1955 replaces every occurrence with __koru_kernel_ptr_<hash>[i] before the loop is printed, and the emit at 2001-2018 interpolates only ptr_name, binding_name and the already-inlined body. Same class as __KORU_INLINE__ above. Its only writer is the standalone kernel:self transform, which today panics before it is even reached (pinned red by 390_056) — but a FIXED transform could not emit this name either, which is why this is an exemption and __koru_kernel_ptr_{} is not
kernel.kz           | __koru_kernel_ptr_{}              | the self_elem substitution's output name — reachable only through the standalone kernel:self transform, which panics before emitting (pinned red by 390_056). Unlike its input sentinel this name WOULD be bare surface once the transform is fixed; the exemption lapses the day 390_056 goes green
compiler.kz         | __test__                          | a synthetic filename handed to Parser.init during test generation (compiler.kz:1431), quoted in a string the extractor reads as emitted text; not emitted code
bridge.bind.kz      | __type_ref                        | field-name sentinel the bridge's introspection verbs compare and serialise into JSON payloads; JSON data, not emitted Zig. Was bridge.hostverbs.kz until the bind part split moved the comparisons; attribution followed the move again
fmt.csprec.kz       | __koru_continue_{}                | template CONTINUATION MARKER, not emitted code: several modules (fmt, regex, switch, trellis) write it into a flow's inline_body, and src/emitter_helpers.zig:4296 emitInlineCodeResolvingSplices replaces every occurrence with that continuation's body before anything is written (js_emitter.zig:365 does the same for the JS target). The only path that leaves it verbatim is the `unresolvable; loud` fallback at emitter_helpers.zig:4374, which writes an undefined identifier Zig rejects — so no PASSING program can carry it. The derivation names ONE site per symbol; a file-keyed exemption over a multi-file symbol goes stale whenever scan order moves — attribution now lands on fmt.csprec.kz
channel.kz          | __channel_decl_{}                 | decl marker emitted by markerItem as a `// __channel_decl_<name> vocab=...` host_line — comment-carried, the scan strips it by construction
channel.kz          | __channel_anchor                  | dedup anchor: an event_decl spliced into the channel module_decl; it materialises only as the `__channel_anchor_event` handler struct (fullmatch fails) and inside string literals/comment lines — the bare name never reaches code
rings.new.kz        | __rings_decl_{}                   | decl marker emitted by markerItem as a `// __rings_decl_<name> elem=...` host_line — comment-carried, the scan strips it by construction
rings.new.kz        | __rings_anchor                    | dedup anchor: an event_decl spliced into the rings module_decl; materialises only as `__rings_anchor_event` (fullmatch fails) and inside string literals — the bare name never reaches code. Verified 2026-10-21 against 320_090's artifact: 4 textual hits, all comment-or-string
rings.new.kz        | __ring_{}_enqueue                 | synthOp name, not emitted surface: the op body emits as the `__ring_<n>_enqueue_event` handler struct (fullmatch fails) and its name appears verbatim only inside `// >>> PROC` comments the scan strips. Verified 2026-10-21 against 320_103's artifact
rings.new.kz        | __ring_{}_dequeue                 | same shape as __ring_{}_enqueue — the dequeue op materialises as `__ring_<n>_dequeue_event` plus `// >>> PROC` comments; the bare name never reaches code
fmt.kz              | __BlkResult                       | dead union arm: emitted only when the fmt.blk site has NO return binding, and unbound consumption produces Zig the backend rejects — verified 2026-10-21 (`expected '[]const u8', found '__BlkResult'` + auto-discharge trying to free the union). No PASSING program can carry it. Latent defect: unbound blk should refuse like 620_006's ruling, not leak a raw Zig type error
fmt.lnzig.kz        | __LnResult                        | dead union arm: emitted only for a `| line l` branch consume — a legacy router-inline spelling the bare-return grammar refuses — or for unbound use, which like __BlkResult emits Zig the backend rejects. No PASSING program can carry it

# --- JS-target output: lands in output_emitted.js, which this check does not scan ---
parser.kz           | __he{}                            | std/parser JS-target generator (`===` in the template); its output is output_emitted.js, outside the Zig artifact scan
parser.kz           | __hv{}                            | std/parser JS-target generator; same site family as __he{}
parser.kz           | __koru_lit_eq                     | std/parser JS-target literal comparator (parser.kz:868, JS `===` template); the Zig dual __koru_lit_eq_{} is covered
parser.kz           | __koru_main_{}                    | std/parser JS-target entrypoint (`function __koru_main_{s}()`, process.argv); JS output only
store.hostemit.kz   | __g                               | std/store ref-home JS guard's generation extraction (`const __g = Math.floor(__v / 4294967296)`); emitted only into output_emitted.js, outside the Zig artifact scan — the Zig and CS duals carry their own sites. Was store.refhome.kz until the hostemit part split moved the guard; attribution followed the move
regex.kz            | __koru_match_buf_{}_{}            | |js arm of std/regex match — the subject copied into a `Buffer.from(...)`; Zig match emits __koru_match_in_/__koru_re_ which are covered (810_021)
regex.kz            | __koru_re_int_{}_{}               | |js arm int-group coercion helper (`Number.isInteger` guard); only minted when a `|int|`-style field needs it under the JS target
regex.scan.kz       | __koru_scan_buf_{}_{}             | |js arm of std/regex scan — same Buffer.from subject copy as the match twin; Zig scan carries its own covered names
regex.scan.kz       | __koru_re_scan_int_{}_{}          | |js arm int-group coercion helper for scan; JS-target only

# --- CS-target output: lands in output_emitted.cs, which this check does not scan ---
io.csprec.kz        | __koru_stderr_write               | |cs placeholder-write verb name, selected when to_fd == 2 in the CS print engine; C# text only
io.blkcs.kz         | __koru_stdout_write               | |cs block-print write verb; C# text only
store.csemit.kz     | __slot                            | inside the `__koru_row_of` C# handle-decoder body (`public static long`); C# text only
store.csemit.kz     | __slot32                          | same C# handle-decoder body; C# text only
store.csemit.kz     | __u                               | same C# handle-decoder body; C# text only
store.new.kz        | __h                               | parameter name inside `public static dynamic __koru_read_<f>(long __h)` — the store's CS-target handle-read method; C# text only
store.ixrefs.kz     | __koru_read_{}                    | emitted only under `storeHostTarget() == .cs` — the per-field handle-read call spelled as a method; the Zig arm resolves handles inline under different names
store.query.kz      | __koru_firstblk_done              | the `host_is_cs` arm's `goto __koru_firstblk_done` first-block jump label; the Zig arm's label is plain `firstblk`
